{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Vajjita","html":"<article id='thag2.48'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.48 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.48 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Pañcamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Five </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Vajjitattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Vajjita </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Saṁsaraṁ dīghamaddhānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Transmigrating for such a long time, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>gatīsu parivattisaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve cycled through various states of rebirth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Apassaṁ ariyasaccāni, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>not seeing the noble truths, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>andhabhūto puthujjano. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a blind, unenlightened person. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tassa me appamattassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>But when I became heedful, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>saṁsārā vinaḷīkatā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>transmigrations were mown down. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sabbā gatī samucchinnā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>All states of rebirth are cut off; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi dāni punabbhavo”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>now there’ll be no more future lives. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Vajjito thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
